tions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"If there's some safety related issue here, I'm not sure how that'd work, I'm not very experienced with C++.\r\n\r\nIn theory, when `play_stream()` is called and there are no streams playing, `active_ids` will be empty. Otherwise, it should always have at least one item. At the end of the same method, successful calls will generate an ID and that ID will be added to the vector. Otherwise, the method returns `INVALID_ID` and nothing new is added to the vector.\r\n\r\nIndividual items are only removed when the relevant stream is done, or stops (this include internal stops due to `STOP_OLDEST`). `active_ids` is only fully cleared when `AudioStreamPolyphonic` is stopped. AFAIK, that stream will always be running unless `stop()` is called on it.\r\n\r\nI haven't debugged, but I and a friend have tested. I think the only assumption I make here, is that there'll always be a `mix()` call between `play_stream()` calls, so `active_ids` Will never be bigger than `streams.size()`.","created_at":"2026-07-15T16:10:14Z","updated_at":"2026-07-15T16:10:14Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120761#discussion_r3588908591","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120761","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3588908591"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120761#discussion_r3588908591"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120761"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3588908591/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":239,"original_line":239,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3585461518,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":80,"position":80,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3588927196","pull_request_review_id":4706017786,"id":3588927196,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7V6q7c","diff_hunk":"@@ -212,6 +235,16 @@ AudioStreamPlaybackPolyphonic::ID AudioStreamPlaybackPolyphonic::play_stream(con\n \t\t\t? AudioServer::get_singleton()->get_default_playback_type()\n \t\t\t: p_playback_type;\n \n+\tif (polyphony_mode_playback == AudioStreamPolyphonic::STOP_OLDEST && active_ids.size() == streams.size()) {\n+\t\tStream *s = _find_stream(active_ids[0]);","path":"scene/resources/audio/audio_stream_polyphonic.cpp","commit_id":"126e65958b92ce774789f51d4aca79ddd32342a4","original_commit_id":"2d699461c1dfdca8bf8ff8760ea55e5aebd0915f","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'd 